            "content_descriptors": {
                "ids": [
                    5
                ],
                "notes": "\"Urban Pirate\" is a visual story that, with self-irony, portrays the tragicomic life of a young, anti-authoritarian rebel in a Western city during the 2000s. The main character must steal from supermarkets, scavenge through dumpsters, smoke marijuana, skateboard, live in an abandoned house with his squatter friends, throw Molotov cocktails at police forces, and struggle against the local authorities just to get through everyday life.\r\n\r\nAlthough the story is humorous and self-ironic, this may be difficult for younger audiences to understand. The game is not recommended for younger players or for those who wish to avoid themes of crime, drugs, tobacco, or questionable morals.\r\n\r\nThere are one or two brief animations in which the main character is attacked by a gang member, and in a few scenes, he is pinned to the ground during an arrest. When the character falls off his skateboard, a minor nosebleed may also occur."
            },
